Over the past 20 years, the \cls{beamer} class~[3] has become the
standard for production of presentations with \LaTeX{}. This class can produce
a wide range of visual effects, and it has proved itself to be extremely useful
for the creation of presentations. However, the internal code of \cls{beamer}
is very complex and somewhat idiosyncratic. The class focuses primarily on the
visual output, with structures reused in a way that makes it difficult to see
how tagging data can be added. Finally, some aspects of the user interface in
\cls{beamer} deviate significantly from standard \LaTeX{} constructs and
conventions.
